.TH "waybar\-image" "5" "2026\-08\-07"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- image module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBimage\fR module displays container of images(or image) from a provided paths
.PP
.SH REMARK
.PP
This module has been rewritten to add multiple image rendering functionality.\&
To avoid users inconvenience of breaking changes, everything related to old(only
one \fBimage\fR) implementation has been left untouched including configuration part.\& For this
reason this wiki page is split into two parts
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
For single \fBimage\fR
.PP
\fBpath\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
The path to the image.\&
.PP
\fBexec\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
The path to the script, which should return image path file.\& 
.br
It will only execute if the path is not set
.PP
\fBsize\fR: 
.br
typeof: integer 
.br
The width/height to render the image.\&
.PP
\fBinterval\fR: 
.br
typeof: integer or float 
.br
The interval (in seconds) to re\-render the image.\& 
.br
If set to a positive value, the minimum is 0.\&001 (1ms).\& Values smaller than 1ms will be set to 1ms.\& 
.br
Zero or negative values are treated as "once".\& 
.br
This is useful if the contents of \fBpath\fR changes.\& 
.br
If no \fBinterval\fR is defined, the image will only be rendered once.\&
.PP
\fBsignal\fR: 
.br
typeof: integer 
.br
The signal number used to update the module.\& 
.br
This can be used instead of \fBinterval\fR if the file changes irregularly.\& 
.br
The number is valid between 1 and N, where \fBSIGRTMIN+N\fR = \fBSIGRTMAX\fR.\&
.PP
\fBon\-click\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when clicked on the module.\&
.PP
\fBon\-click\-middle\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when middle\-clicked on the module using mousewheel.\&
.PP
\fBon\-update\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when the module is updated.\&
.PP
\fBon\-scroll\-up\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when scrolling up on the module.\&
.PP
\fBon\-scroll\-down\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when scrolling down on the module.\&
.PP
\fBsmooth\-scrolling\-threshold\fR: 
.br
typeof: double 
.br
Threshold to be used when scrolling.\&
.PP
\fBtooltip\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: true 
.br
Option to enable tooltip on hover.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables this module to consume all left over space dynamically.\&
.PP
.SH SCRIPT OUTPUT
.PP
Similar to the \fBcustom\fR module, output values of the script are \fBnewline\fR separated.\&
The following is the output format:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
$path\\n$tooltip
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"image#album\-art": {
	"path": "/tmp/mpd_art",
	"size": 32,
	"interval": 5,
	"on\-click": "mpc toggle"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Using \fBexec\fR to fetch the image via a script:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"image#album\-art": {
	"exec": "~/\&.config/waybar/custom/spotify/album_art\&.sh",
	"size": 32,
	"interval": 30
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where \fBalbum_art.\&sh\fR looks like this:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
#!/bin/bash
album_art=$(playerctl \-p spotify metadata mpris:artUrl)
if [[ \-z $album_art ]]; then
	# spotify is dead, we should die too\&.
	exit
fi
curl \-s "${album_art}" \-\-output "/tmp/cover\&.jpeg"
echo "/tmp/cover\&.jpeg"
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH STYLE
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#image\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#image.\&empty\fR
.PD
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
For multiple \fBimage\fR
.PP
\fBsize\fR: 
.br
typeof: integer 
.br
default: 16 
.br
Minumum size of the rendered image in pixels.\&
.PP
\fBinterval\fR: 
.br
typeof: integer or float 
.br
The interval (in seconds) to re\-render the module.\& 
.br
If set to a positive value, the minimum is 0.\&001 (1ms).\& Values smaller than 1ms will be set to 1ms.\& 
.br
Zero or negative values (and the literal "once") are treated as "once".\& 
.br
This is useful if image path or other property is being changed over time.\& 
.br
If no \fBinterval\fR is provided, the module will only be rendered once.\&
.PP
\fBmultiple\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
this parameter is used to decide if old \fBimage\fR implementation should be 
.br
used(therefore render only one image) or to pick a new implementation to 
.br
rended multiple images provided from this config.\& default value of this 
.br
parameter is false.\&
.PP
\fBsignal\fR: 
.br
typeof: interger 
.br
default: 0 
.br
The signal number is used to redraw the module.\& 
.br
This is used if \fBinterval\fR is not provided and module should change 
.br
regularly depended on external events, e.\&g when clicking on it.\& 
.br
The provided value is valid between 1 and N, where SIGRTMIN+N <= SIGRTMAX.\& 
.br
e.\&g if \fBsignal\fR = 7, 34 + 7 = 41, which means waybar process should	
.br
receive signal 41 to redraw this module, since SIGRTMIN = 34 (see '\&kill \-l'\&).\&
.PP
\fBentries\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
default: empty array 
.br
Json array of objects consisting of several fields 
.br
this is a main part of configuration where per image properties are defined
.PP
.RS 4
\fBpath\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: empty string 
.br
file path of picture to draw
.PP
\fBmarker\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: empty string 
.br
user defined per image keyword(marker) to identify them, e.\&g in styles.\&css 
.br
e.\&g if you want to draw 3 pictures and one of them dimmed, you can give 
.br
\fBmarker\fR: "dimmed" value and in styles.\&css write something like this 
.br
#image .\&dimmed { opacity: 0.\&3 }
.PP
\fBtooltip\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: empty string 
.br
description of the image displayed on hover
.PP
\fBon\-click\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: empty string 
.br
action to perform when clicking on the image.\& 
.br
The action can be any system or custom binary/script 
.br
e.\&g if { "on\-click": "notify\-send "hello world"" } 
.br
"hello world" will appear as notification.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBexec\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: empty string 
.br
same as \fBentries\fR but provided from external script which should dynamically 
.br
return json array of objects consisting of same keys as \fBentries\fR.\& 
.br
This option is specifically useful in combination with \fBsignal\fR option without \fBinterval\fR provided.\&
.PP
.SH Examples
.PP
With entries
.nf
.RS 4
"image#wentr": {
  "entries": [
    {
      "path": "/home/user/Pictures/idk1\&.png",
      "marker": "dimmed",
      "tooltip": "dimmed image",
      "on\-click": "notify\-send "hello world""
    },
    {
      "path": "/home/user/Pictures/idk2\&.png",
      "marker": "normal",
      "on\-click": "myCustomScript\&.py"
    }
  ],
  "size": 32,
  "interval": 1 // will redraw every 5 seconds
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
With exec
.nf
.RS 4
"image#wexec": {
  "exec": "imageProvider\&.py",
  "size": 32,
  "signal": 7 // e\&.g \&'pkill \-n waybar \-\-signal 41\&' will trigger redraw
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
where imageProvider.\&py looks like this
.nf
.RS 4
#!/usr/bin/python

import json

dir = "/home/user/Pictures/"
out = [
    {"path": dir + "idk1\&.png", "marker": "clickable", "on\-click": "echo \&'hello world\&'"},
    {"path": dir + "idk2\&.png", "marker": "normal", "tooltip": "sample tooltip"},
    {"path": dir + "idk3\&.png", "marker": "important"},
]
res = json\&.dumps(out)
print(res)
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SS Example styles
.nf
.RS 4
#image \&.important {
    opacity: 0\&.9;
}

#image button\&.important {
    opacity: 0\&.2
}

#image \&.normal {
    opacity: 0\&.3
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH STYLE
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#image\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#image\fR.\&empty /*when image could not be rendered*/
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#image\fR button /*when on\-click is provided; a Gtk::Button is matched by the element selector, not a class*/
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#image\fR.\&\fBmarker\fR /*where \fBmarker\fR is parameter from config*/
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#image\fR button.\&\fBmarker\fR
.PD
.PP
